# Optional — append "azelow" to whichever spawn group fits the in-game distribution
# you want. cargrp.dat lives at data/cargrp.dat. Each line is "groupname, car1, car2, ...".
# Example: append the new car to the "rich" / "executive" group.
#
# (If you only spawn the car via the server-side filterscript, you can skip this.)
#
# Replace one of the existing rich-family lines, e.g.:
#   rich, admiral, premier, sentinel, washington, ...
# with:
#   rich, admiral, premier, sentinel, washington, ..., azelow
